<title>UK: S.Electric says windfall tax is &quot;political&quot;.</title>
<headline>S.Electric says windfall tax is &quot;political&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British regional electricity company (Rec) Southern Electric Plc said on Wednesday that the new Labour government's proposed &quot;windfall&quot; tax was &quot;political.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;The windfall tax is a political tax,&quot; finance director Ian Marchant told Reuters in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>He said the company had made its views known to the Treasury &quot;in a constructive way,&quot; but details would remain private.</p>
<p>The government has vowed to introduce a one-off tax on &quot;excess profits&quot; of privatised utilities to fund a three billion pound plan to cut unemployment as a major plank of its first budget, scheduled for July 2.</p>
<p>Companies were asked to submit comments by the end of May, with regulators being heard over the next two weeks.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
